CDDA 0.I: avoid linear monster tracking scans on every move and remove
small-set heap churn from per-turn vehicle item processing.

1. creature_tracker::update_pos already has an old-position hash index. When
that index points at the moving monster, use it to re-key the entry directly.
Retain the upstream vector search/rebuild recovery path when the index does not
match, and do not change monster list order or any movement/AI work.
2. map::process_items builds a temporary tree set of vehicle submaps every turn.
For up to 32 vehicles, collect coordinates in a fixed stack array, sort and
deduplicate them to preserve std::set's visitation order, and process them.
For larger populations, preserve the existing std::set path to avoid an
unbounded stack buffer.
